{
  "id": "ep216",
  "duration": 44.033,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.229,
      "text": "You do not need 25,000 miles per hour to escape Earth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Earth seen from Apollo 17.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Apollo 17 crew; taken by either Harrison Schmitt or Ron Evans",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Earth_seen_from_Apollo_17.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.967,
          "end": 4.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.229,
      "end": 11.799,
      "text": "That terrifying speed limit is actually just a mathematical shortcut for a single unpowered ballistic burst.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "SaturnV S-IVB.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SaturnV_S-IVB.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.233,
          "end": 8.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.0,
          "end": 11.8,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.799,
      "end": 19.244,
      "text": "If you fire a projectile and let gravity do all the work, you genuinely need 11.2 kilometers per second.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Apollo 11 Launch - GPN-2000-000630.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apollo_11_Launch_-_GPN-2000-000630.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.8,
          "end": 19.233,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.244,
      "end": 22.494,
      "text": "But spacecraft are not simple cannonballs.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "STS120LaunchHiRes-edit1.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA; edited by jjron (tilt corrected)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:STS120LaunchHiRes-edit1.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.233,
          "end": 22.5,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 22.494,
      "end": 30.164,
      "text": "By keeping their powerful engines burning, they can climb slowly at a leisurely walking pace and still slip away completely.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "STS-134 International Space Station after undocking.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:STS-134_International_Space_Station_after_undocking.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 22.5,
          "end": 26.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 26.333,
          "end": 30.167,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.164,
      "end": 36.939,
      "text": "Escape velocity is not a strict speed limit you must break, but merely an underlying energy bill.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Periods Slika 02 b.jpg",
        "credit": "Ivan T.",
        "license": "CC BY 3.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Periods_Slika_02_b.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.167,
          "end": 36.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.939,
      "end": 43.683,
      "text": "Thanks to continuous thrust provided by onboard propellants, you never have to pay that massive bill all at once.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Earth seen from Apollo 17.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Apollo 17 crew; taken by either Harrison Schmitt or Ron Evans",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Earth_seen_from_Apollo_17.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.933,
          "end": 44.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
